    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Role in SSc:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " tocilizumab (anti-IL-6) preserves lung funct in SSc-ILD; becoming an alt to mycophenolate, esp w predom polyarthritis; rituximab = being evaluated for CTD-ILD and may have efficacy; skin: tocilizumab and rituximab (among others) have shown modest benefit."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Tocilizumab (Actemra) dose, systemic sclerosis-associated ILD (SSc-ILD):"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " SSc-ILD: 162 mg Q1wk SC."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Tocilizumab (Actemra) boxed warning:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " ↑ risk of serious infect that may lead to hsp or death; most pts were taking concomitant immunosuppressants such as MTX or corticosteroids. Test for latent TB b4 ACTEMRA use and during therapy (except pts w COVID-19); start tx for latent infect prior to ACTEMRA use."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Tocilizumab (Actemra) CI:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " known hypersensitivity to ACTEMRA."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Tocilizumab (Actemra) GI perf:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " GI perf reported, primarily as comp of diverticulitis; use w caution in pts who may be @ ↑ risk; promptly evaluate fever, new onset abd Sx, and a Δ in bowel habits for early identification."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Tocilizumab (Actemra) hepatotoxicity:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " Obtain liver test panel (ALT, AST, AP, total bili) b4 ACTEMRA and every 4 to 8 wks for the first 6 mo, then every 3 mo; ⍉ initiate in RA, GCA or SSc-ILD pts w ALT or AST > 1.5× ULN; d/c if ALT or AST > 5× ULN."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Tocilizumab (Actemra) lab monitoring:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " ⍉ initiate in RA, GCA and SSc-ILD pts w ANC < 2000 per mm3; if ANC < 500 per mm3 tx = ⍉recommended. ⍉ initiate in RA, GCA and SSc-ILD pts w PLT below 100,000 per mm3; if PLT < 50,000 per mm3 tx = ⍉recommended. Assess lipid parameters ≈ 4 to 8 wks following initiation of ACTEMRA."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Tocilizumab (Actemra) live vax:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " ⍉ use of live vax concurrently w ACTEMRA."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Tocilizumab (Actemra) CYP450 interaction:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " Inhibition of IL-6 signaling in RA pts treated w tocilizumab may restore CYP450 activities to higher levels than in the absence of tocilizumab, leading to ↑ met of CYP450 substrate drugs. On initiation or discontinuation of ACTEMRA, perform therapeutic monitoring of effect (ex, warfarin) or drug concentration (ex, cyclosporine or theophylline) and adjust the dose prn."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Rituximab (Rituxan) IV boxed warning — infusion rxns:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " Fatal infusion-related rxns w/in 24 h of RITUXAN infusion; ≈ 80% of fatal rxns occurred w first infusion; monitor pts and d/c RITUXAN infusion for severe rxns."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Rituximab (Rituxan) IV boxed warning — mucocut rxns:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " Severe mucocut rxns, some w fatal outcomes."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Rituximab (Rituxan) IV boxed warning — HBV reactivation:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " HBV reactivation, in some cases resulting in fulminant hepatitis, hepatic failure, and death. Screen all pts for HBV infect b4 tx initiation and monitor pts during and after tx; d/c RITUXAN and concomitant meds in the event of HBV reactivation."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Rituximab (Rituxan) IV boxed warning — PML:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " Progressive multifocal leukoencephalopathy (PML) resulting in death."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Rituximab (Rituxan) IV infect:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " Serious, incl fatal, bact, fungal, and new or reactivated viral infect can occur during and following the completion of RITUXAN-based therapy. D/c RITUXAN for serious infect and institute appropriate anti-infective therapy."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Rituximab (Rituxan) IV ♡ rxns:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " ♡ adverse rxns incl VF, MI, and cardiogenic shock may occur; d/c infusions for serious or life-threatening ♡ arrhythmias; perform ♡ monitoring during and after all infusions in pts who develop clinically sig arrhythmias or who have a Hx of arrhythmia or angina."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Rituximab (Rituxan) IV live vax:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " Vax w live virus vax = ⍉recommended b4 or during tx; administer non live vax at least 4 wks prior to a course of RITUXAN."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
